      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Kast's first cabinet reshuffle at 69 days triggers approval drop, broad opposition criticism, and coalition friction",
      "summary": "President Kast replaced Security Minister Trinidad Steinert and spokesperson Mara Sedini 69 days into his administration, appointing Mart\u00edn Arrau to Security and consolidating Claudio Alvarado as biminister of Interior and Segegob. Polls showed Kast's approval falling to 32\u201337% and 57% of respondents saying he has not met security expectations, though 72% endorsed the cabinet change itself. Opposition parties across the left called the reshuffle evidence of 'total improvisation,' while Chile Vamos ally Evelyn Matthei publicly questioned the original appointment, triggering a rebuke from Libertad y Desarrollo. The government convened a fourth cabinet council to define a 'second phase' strategy ahead of the June 1 Cuenta P\u00fablica.",
