      "headline": "Codelco production overstatement scandal: executive fired, 6,000 workers ordered to return $14.3M in bonuses, criminal referral filed",
      "summary": "An internal audit at Codelco found that the world's largest copper producer overstated 2025 production by approximately 26,875 tonnes\u2014roughly 2% of annual output\u2014at Chuquicamata and Ministro Hales divisions, allowing year-end targets to be met artificially. The board fired one executive, disciplined several others, and referred the matter to prosecutors. More than 6,000 workers and executives were ordered to return performance bonuses totalling US$14.3 million, prompting unions to threaten work stoppages. Economy Minister Daniel Mas called the situation 'inaceptable' and said 'Codelco is out of control.' Board chair M\u00e1ximo Pacheco departed and was replaced by Bernardo Fontaine, who announced plans for an external KPMG audit.",
